        "original_id": "74a32047-24ff-5a24-9c9b-cd36578b2f69",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Czesław Miłosz, Bhabananda Deka\n- Works: The Captive Mind\n- Roles: poet, prose writer, translator, diplomat, economist, author, academic\n- Places: Poland, Assam, India\n\nFacts:\n- Czesław Miłosz was born on 30 June 1911 and died on 14 August 2004.\n- Czesław Miłosz was a Polish poet, prose writer, translator, and diplomat.\n- Bhabananda Deka was born on 19 August 1929 and died on 4 December 2006.\n- Bhabananda Deka was acknowledged as a pioneering Assamese economist and author who first conducted path-breaking research on the economy of far eastern India.\n- The Captive Mind is a 1953 nonfiction work by Polish writer, academic, and Nobel laureate Czesław Miłosz.\n- The Captive Mind was originally published in English translation by Secker and Warburg.",
